# Renderer

The renderer draws the workflow and sends typed messages. It does not run agents, touch git, or import `@cursor/sdk`.

- Workflow state lives in Zustand. React Flow is a view of that store, not the store itself.
- Illegal connections are rejected by the shared validator. Do not keep a second copy of the type rules in the component.
- Elements a test clicks need `data-testid` in kebab-case.
- jsdom tests must stub `ResizeObserver` and `matchMedia` when a component uses React Flow.

```tsx
// BAD — connection rules reimplemented in the component
if (source.name === "diff") return false;
// GOOD
const error = connectError(workflow, source, target);
```
